  "description": "Shenora's iOS shell: the MAUI HybridWebView IPC transport (the same envelope the desktop shell speaks, over SendRawMessage/RawMessageReceived), the resource interceptor that answers a page's byte ranges, a UI-thread dispatcher, safe-area insets, foreground transitions carrying how long the app was away, and the iOS implementations of the Shenora shell contracts — native file dialogs, an AudioToolbox/VideoToolbox conversion pipeline with device capability probing, an AVPlayer media player, and a Now Playing playback session. The platform owns the loop, so the app drives ShenoraApplication.Start/Stop from its own lifecycle rather than calling Run. Shares its source with Shenora.Android. Also ships the Live Activity devkit: the app writes four SwiftUI view bodies and sets one MSBuild property, and the package supplies the ActivityKit shim, the state mirror and the build step that produces and signs the widget extension.",
